WEBVTT

NOTE Two ways to make six seconds. English captions.

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.022
Now the cue is six seconds.

2
00:00:03.672 --> 00:00:06.141
The original eight-second
approach arrives late.

3
00:00:07.091 --> 00:00:11.220
One fix keeps the six-meter start
and uses one meter per second:

4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.094
y equals negative x plus six.

5
00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:19.245
Another keeps the three-fourths pace
and starts four and a half meters away:

6
00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:22.947
y equals negative three-fourths
x plus four and a half.

7
00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:26.817
Both reach zero distance
remaining at six seconds.

8
00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:31.201
Change one parameter, then
match the equation to your plan.
